WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Speaker 1: I'm not going to spend a ton&nbsp;
of time on this, but Mike Pence has put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:11.280
together a number of appearances here connected,&nbsp;
of course, to the book that he has written. And he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:20.220
you know, he's turned on Trump. He's abandoned&nbsp;
Trump. Pence has put together a list of five or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.500
so very calculated statements that he repeats.&nbsp;
One that we've heard often is what Trump did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:32.280
was reckless on January 6th. Another one that he&nbsp;
repeats is he endangered my family. These are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.860
accidents. These are workshopped lines where&nbsp;
Pence knows he's going to get these questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:43.680
and he works with a team to figure out. Here's&nbsp;
the things I'm going to say. A new thing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:50.340
he said yesterday on Fox News was that there will&nbsp;
be better choices for the Republican nomination in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:55.980
2024 than Trump. And one of the most interesting&nbsp;
things about this is watching the Fox, Fox and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:02.640
Friends hosts figure out how to deal with this.
Speaker 2: I honestly believe that we'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.760
have better choices come 20,&nbsp;
24. You know, I don't think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.700
anybody questions that Donald Trump. I do. Yeah.
Speaker 1: We will have better choices than Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:18.780
Trump. So the question still remains, of course,&nbsp;
if the nominee in 24 is Donald Trump, will you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.780
vote? Vote for him? I have no reason right now to&nbsp;
believe that the answer is no. I think much like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:30.420
William Barr, who criticized Trump up and down&nbsp;
for a dozen different things. And then when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.960
came to, well, but would you vote for him if he's&nbsp;
the nominee? And he's like, Well, yeah, Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.120
are a disaster. I'm not voting for a Democrat. I&nbsp;
think despite all this, despite Pence's anger that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.580
Trump endangered his family, he still hasn't said&nbsp;
If Trump is the nominee, I will not vote for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.020
and I think that he will. One other interesting&nbsp;
anecdote from yesterday's interview with Fox.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.049
He talked about, I guess my understanding&nbsp;
is this is the last time he spoke to Trump.&nbsp;

00:01:54.049 --> 00:02:01.680
Speaker 2: And I went into his office and I after&nbsp;
he made inquiries about Karen and Charlotte,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.660
who'd been with me at the Capitol the entire&nbsp;
time on January six. All the way till four in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:13.440
the morning. Yeah. He asked me. He asked me what&nbsp;
I'd felt that day and I told him I was angry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:20.880
We had our differences, and seeing those&nbsp;
people ransacking the Capitol infuriated me. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:28.020
my my only thought was not this not here, not&nbsp;
in America. Right. But we I was very candid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:32.640
with him. We were very straightforward with each&nbsp;
other. I sensed in the president as a right of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:40.380
genuine remorse about what had happened in the&nbsp;
days that followed, that we spoke again and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.100
again in the two weeks remaining of the events.
Speaker 1: What's funny about I sense genuine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:49.320
remorse is as recently as last month or two&nbsp;
weeks ago, Trump made clear he doesn't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:54.720
remorse. He repeated all the same stuff that&nbsp;
infuriated his followers about Mike Pence. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.820
also Trump has never expressed remorse about&nbsp;
anything. None of this all seems made up.&nbsp;

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:06.540
Speaker 2: But on that day that you ask&nbsp;
about, I sense the president was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.640
saddened by what had occurred. And I just&nbsp;
reminded him, as I had at the beginning of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.140
our first conversation, that I was praying&nbsp;
for him. I prayed for that president almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:25.980
every day during our administration, and he&nbsp;
was dismissive about it at first. It don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:32.100
don't bother. But then as a few minutes later,&nbsp;
as I got up to leave the room, I looked at him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.700
as he said at the end of the little table in&nbsp;
the dining room, just off the Oval Office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.680
And I said, Well, I guess there's just two things&nbsp;
we're probably always going to disagree on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:48.960
And he looked up at me and faintly said, What?&nbsp;
And I said, referred to my role on January six.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:56.100
And then I said, I'm never going to stop&nbsp;
praying for you. And he looked at me and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.269
and said, That's right. Don't don't ever&nbsp;
change. Know that we parted amicably.&nbsp;

00:04:02.269 --> 00:04:07.620
Speaker 1: Does anybody believe that story? And&nbsp;
the biggest lie seems to be the last thing. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:14.640
parted amicably. Trump doesn't part amicably with&nbsp;
people. He just doesn't. I don't believe a word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:19.380
of that story. So it's an interesting&nbsp;
anecdote because it's the opposite of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:25.080
everything that we know Trump to be. He wants&nbsp;
to sell books. We'll see what happens in 2024

